WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:05.000
Lesson 9.9 · Financial Management
Audit, examination and financial governance

2
00:00:05.600 --> 00:00:11.800
Your board oversees the money: it knows the external checks and sets a reserves target.

3
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.600
1. Confirm which audit or examination applies to you.

4
00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:18.200
2. Set what the board reviews and approves, and when.

5
00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:22.200
3. Write a reserves target, the reason and actions.

6
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:23.800
An example: Vanita Weavers Cooperative (Cooperative · member-owned, India)

7
00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:31.000
“Vanita: audited yearly by the state department; members approve the accounts in September; reserve target US$13,000, now US$1,500.”

8
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:33.400
You write your scrutiny, board oversight and reserves policy.

9
00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:37.400
Then save it, and download it as a PDF.

10
00:00:38.900 --> 00:00:42.000
Method into Impact
Better foundations. Stronger organisations.
